From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: accept valid DP and USB assignments

The Uke unknown-mode guard was added to a fallback shared with assignments
D and F. It rejects those valid DP+USB modes before the PHY can leave USB.
The Type-C mux framework ignores EOPNOTSUPP from an individual provider,
so the WCD switch can report DP while QMP silently retains USB-only routing.

Select USB3DP explicitly for D/F and keep the Uke rejection for unknown
assignments. Retain all power, route-error and active-DP guards. This restores
the upstream mode selection without changing PHY tables or board values.

--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -4884,6 +4884,8 @@
 		/* DP + USB */
 		case TYPEC_DP_STATE_D:
 		case TYPEC_DP_STATE_F:
+			new_mode = QMPPHY_MODE_USB3DP;
+			break;
 
 		/* Safe fallback...*/
 		default:
